  "req_ids": ["DAT-004", "DAT-004a", "DAT-005b"],
  "description": "A screen identity row and a device row, each carrying the full resource-row baseline and a scope_node placement, are accepted — and both are placed under nodes that are NOT screen-kind (the screen under a group, the device under the site), which is the placement freedom DAT-004 grants and the reason a screen_id cannot be read as the id of the screen-kind node a screen happens to sit under. The screen's own id is what a screen_id names and the device's own id is what a device_id names (DAT-004a), so neither is any of the scope-node ids present in the same fixture: the case asserts that separation directly rather than leaving it to convention.",
